Third-party content
-------------------

The parameter descriptions in `spec/effects.toml`, and the tables generated from
them in `docs/effects.md`, are taken from section 9.3 of the DeepMind 12 User
Manual, published by Music Tribe. They are reproduced so that a program can tell
a musician what a parameter does, which is what the protocol data on its own
cannot convey.

The colours in `spec/layout.toml` were measured from the effect panels pictured
in the same section: three colours per effect, taken by ranking the picture's
own colours by how much of it they cover. The result is nine bytes per effect
and no artwork. The drawings in `docs/diagrams/fx/` are generated from that
measurement and from the parameter tables; they are not traced from, and do not
resemble, Behringer's panels.

Everything else in `spec/` is factual interface data: parameter numbers, byte
offsets, names, ranges, units, value lists, and where the synthesizer's own
display puts a control. Facts about how a device behaves are not themselves
creative work, and recording them is what makes an independent implementation
possible.

If Music Tribe or Behringer would prefer the descriptions or the sampled colours
were not reproduced here, open an issue and they will be removed. Nothing else in
this repository depends on either: both are optional fields, and the library
works without them.
